{"header":{"deal":"Renewing customer with international markets","ae":"Elena","acv":null,"outcome":"Lost","scope":"Lost: international traffic moved to local acquiring; the US business stayed with us.","competitor":"Adyen","incumbent":"Us (Stripe)","tag":"Approval rates","runner_up":"Support and service","tag_why":"Stefan compared approval performance by country, card type and issuer against Adyen's real-traffic test results, and we answered with an average uplift instead of his own numbers until after the test had finished."},
 "sections":{
  "trigger":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E1","excerpt":"A new head of payments. Stefan. They'd never had one.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E2","excerpt":"Payments sat under an engineering manager, the guy who originally bought us, and he left last year.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E4","excerpt":"the first thing he did was pull declines by country.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E27","excerpt":"I didn't know they'd hired a head of payments.","label":"fact"}],"insight":"No product problem was reported before the evaluation started. It started because a new owner applied a lens we had never shown this account: declines by country. Our champion left last year and we never noticed the replacement, so the account looked 'healthy' only because nobody was measuring what Stefan measured. Our global positioning lost exactly in the international markets, Brazil and 'a couple in Europe', and we still don't know which European markets or what his numbers showed.","messaging":"Back M1's 'grow globally, in every currency' with a proactive per-market approval readout, delivered whenever a new payments owner appears, so the first decline pull a new leader runs is one we already ran with them."},
  "decider":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E8","excerpt":"Stefan recommended it and the CFO approved.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E9","excerpt":"this went to the CFO two weeks ago.","label":"quote"},{"id":"E16","excerpt":"I can't take an average to my CFO.","label":"quote"}],"insight":"The real audience was a CFO we only hear about through Stefan. The transcript doesn't establish that we ever spoke to the CFO. We learned the recommendation had already gone up only on our last call, so the decision moved past us without our knowledge. Stefan told us the format the CFO needed: his company's own figures, not a benchmark. That is the clearest buying-criteria signal in the whole review.","messaging":"Build the acceptance story as a CFO-ready artifact with the customer's own approvals by market and the money attached, not a deck of averages a champion can't forward."},
  "competitor":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E10","excerpt":"Adyen ran a test on a slice of their international traffic and came back with results by country.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E11","excerpt":"local acquiring.","label":"quote"},{"id":"E12","excerpt":"I can't tell you what the test showed. He wouldn't share it.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E13","excerpt":"They got very specific. What's our approval rate in this country, on this card type, by issuer. And why.","label":"fact"}],"insight":"Adyen didn't win on a claim. It won on a test against the customer's own traffic, which reset Stefan's standard of proof to country, card type and issuer, with a reason for each. We don't know what the test showed, so any belief that Adyen's approvals were better is unverified. What we do know is that their format beat our format. 'Local acquiring' became Stefan's frame, and the rep says she had no counter to it.","messaging":"When a buyer says 'local acquiring', answer with an offer to measure their own international traffic by country and issuer within days, and equip reps with a tested response to the local-acquiring argument."},
  "message":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E14","excerpt":"The Authorization Boost deck. The average uplift customers see.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E15","excerpt":"that's an average. What's mine?","label":"quote"},{"id":"E21","excerpt":"I offered a roadmap session and he didn't take it.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E32","excerpt":"He said it was the most useful thing we'd sent him.","label":"fact"}],"insight":"The rep says 'we weren't really pitching', but we did pitch M4 and it was rejected outright. The roadmap offer was declined too. The only thing that landed was the custom analysis of his own data, which shows the content was right and the timing and format were wrong. The developer and billing goodwill the rep credits for keeping the US is her own read, not something Stefan said.","messaging":"Replace M4's average-uplift claim with 'here are your approvals by market and what we'd fix', and make the payments-performance analysis the default renewal motion instead of a rescue."},
  "decided":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E22","excerpt":"I don't think there was a moment. It was kind of decided before we got in the room.","label":"opinion"},{"id":"E29","excerpt":"But that landed three weeks after he asked, and by then the test was finished.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E31","excerpt":"Real findings. Things we could have fixed.","label":"opinion"},{"id":"E24","excerpt":"When the renewal notice went out and Stefan replied asking to split the contract.","label":"fact"}],"insight":"The rep's view that nothing could be done conflicts with her own account. Stefan asked for exactly what we eventually delivered and called it our most useful work, but it arrived three weeks later, after Adyen's test was done. The turning point looks like that three-week gap, not some decision made before we arrived. It is unclear whether our analysis reached him before or after the recommendation went to the CFO.","messaging":"Make per-market approval analysis a same-week response to any decline-by-country question, because in a head-to-head test the first credible answer on the customer's own data sets the frame."},
  "gaps":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E28","excerpt":"A market-by-market view of their own approval rates, with reasons.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E30","excerpt":"He asked who at Stripe looks at his numbers every month, and I didn't have a name.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E37","excerpt":"I heard from Stripe when I said I was leaving.","label":"quote"}],"insight":"Both gaps are about service, not features. We could produce the analysis but not on demand, and we had no named person watching his numbers each month. M5 sells tiered response times, which answers 'how fast do you reply to a ticket'. Stefan asked 'who is watching me'. His line about hearing from us only when he said he was leaving shows how our coverage looked to him.","messaging":"Add a named, recurring owner of the customer's approval performance (a monthly review with a person's name on it) to the support story alongside M5's response-time tiers."},
  "language":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E33","excerpt":"Money left on the table.","label":"quote"},{"id":"E34","excerpt":"Local cards, local rails.","label":"quote"},{"id":"E35","excerpt":"what's mine.","label":"quote"},{"id":"E36","excerpt":"He doesn't say 'authorization,' he says 'approvals.'","label":"fact"}],"insight":"Stefan describes a revenue leak in his own markets ('money left on the table', 'what's mine'). We describe a product feature ('Authorization Boost', 'Adaptive Acceptance') in vocabulary he doesn't use. 'Local cards, local rails' is a mechanism he can picture, while machine-learning uplift is a mechanism he has to trust. The competitor's language matched his mental model and ours didn't.","messaging":"Rewrite M4 in buyer language, roughly: see the approvals you're losing in each market and the money behind them, using 'approvals' rather than 'authorization rates'."}
 },
 "close":{"gaps":[
  {"question":"What was the deal size (ACV)?","kind":"skipped","follow_up":"Ask Elena or deal desk for the ACV before and after the split, including how much international volume moved."},
  {"question":"Which international markets looked bad to Stefan?","kind":"unknown","follow_up":"Ask our payments performance team which markets their analysis flagged, and have Elena ask Stefan whether he will share his decline-by-country pull."},
  {"question":"What did Adyen's test show?","kind":"unknown","follow_up":"Have Elena ask Stefan, now that the decision is made, what the country-level results were and which number convinced the CFO."},
  {"question":"Which part of our pitch got a reaction, and which got silence?","kind":"dodged","follow_up":"Ask Elena what Stefan said, in his words, when he received the payments-performance analysis, and whether anything besides that analysis drew interest."},
  {"question":"When did you first feel this was lost? What happened right before?","kind":"dodged","follow_up":"Ask Elena to put dates on the split request, Stefan's analysis request, Adyen's test ending, our analysis landing and the CFO approval, to see whether our analysis arrived before the recommendation went up."},
  {"question":"Did anyone from our side ever meet the CFO?","kind":"skipped","follow_up":"Ask Elena whether we had any contact with the CFO, and whether our analysis reached the CFO."},
  {"question":"Was the international business confirmed to Adyen, or to another local acquirer?","kind":"skipped","follow_up":"Ask Elena to confirm with Stefan who now processes the international traffic."}
 ],"rep_takeaway":"A healthy account with no tickets can still be at risk. When the person who bought us leaves, treat the account as open: find the new owner, run their numbers by market before they do, and put a name on who watches them every month. Here our analysis was the most useful thing we sent, but it arrived three weeks late, and that delay cost us more than any gap in the pitch."},
 "confidence":"medium"}
